# 5. COLORFUL BUT CONTROLLED — IMPORTANT

Do not use a single color everywhere.

Do not make every page purple.

Do not use colors only on icons, thin borders, tiny badges, buttons or chart lines.

Instead, use colors in the actual layout and composition.

### Incorporate:

- Large soft colored sections
- Colored hero panels
- Visually distinct page sections
- Soft colored backgrounds behind grouped content
- Illustrated backgrounds
- Colored chart surfaces
- Colored mood selections
- Section-specific visual identities
- Colored timelines
- Layered surfaces
- Meaningful contrast between neutral and colorful areas

Color must be visible immediately when opening the application.

However, do not use every color on every page. Assign colors according to the section's purpose.

### Recommended color balance

Approximately:

- 35% neutral/foundation
- 20% blue
- 15% lavender
- 10% rose
- 10% teal
- 5% amber
- 5% other accents

This is a flexible guide, not a strict formula.

Use colors in a sophisticated manner. Avoid rainbow layouts, excessive gradients, oversaturation and competing colorful panels.

